  "live_records": {
    "q-137101": {
      "dom_id": "step-q137101",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,W=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $W,$ and the vector $b$ above. If the normal equation for the corresponding weighted least-squares problem $W\\,A=Wb$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & 18 \\\\ 18 & b\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b+c?$",
      "worked_solution": "To get the normal equation corresponding to $W\\,Ax=Wb,$ we pre-multiply both sides of the equation by $(W\\,A)^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot W\\,Ax & =(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot Wb \\\\ {A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)Ax & ={A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n{W}^{T}W=[\\begin{aligned}{2}^{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & {1}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & {1}^{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nour normal equation can be written as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}24 & 18 \\\\ 18 & 17\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}18 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=24+17+18=59.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
