    "q-137889": {
      "dom_id": "step-q137889",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Find the solution for the weighted least-squares problem $W\\,Ax=Wb,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,W=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "To get the normal equation corresponding to $W\\,Ax=Wb,$ we pre-multiply both sides of the equation by $(W\\,A)^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot W\\,Ax & =(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot Wb \\\\ {A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)Ax & ={A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n{W}^{T}W=[\\begin{aligned}{1}^{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & {1}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & {2}^{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nour normal equation can be written as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 8 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}17 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-15 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the matrix on the left-hand side is invertible, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & ={[\\begin{aligned}17 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}-15 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{17\\cdot 5-2\\cdot 2}[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 17\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-15 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{81}[\\begin{aligned}-81 \\\\ 81\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
